 <!-- /automd -->
 
+### Rotating the seal password
+
+Set the new secret as `password` and move the previous one to `extraUnsealPasswords`. Sessions sealed with the old password keep working. Sessions are always sealed with `password`, so the extra password only opens sessions and never creates new ones. Cookie sessions are resealed with the new password on their next read, so they migrate by themselves. Sessions read from the session header are not migrated (there is no cookie to rewrite): they keep working while the old password is listed, and expire normally.
+
+To rotate:
+
+1. Set the new password as `password` and move the old one to `extraUnsealPasswords`.
+2. Wait for the period in which cookie sessions are read, long enough for active sessions to be resealed. Sessions from the session header only end when they expire, so the window must cover their lifetime too.
+3. Remove the old password from `extraUnsealPasswords`.
+
